OL,3,GNEWSA'Tone deaf at best' - advice to
OL,4,Astock up on essentials worries experts
OL,5,Aand low-income families
OL,6,
OL,7,FLast week, Wes Streeting said people
OL,8,Fshould have water, tinned goods, baby
OL,9,Ffood, torches and mobile phone charging
OL,10,Fpacks ready in case of emergency.
OL,12,FBut one professor said the guidance
OL,13,F"will appear at best tone deaf and at
OL,14,Fworst almost insulting" to households
OL,15,Ffacing poverty.
